<title>AUSTRIA: MOTOR RACING-BERGER TO MISS FRENCH GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-BERGER TO MISS FRENCH GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Formula One driver Gerhard Berger has withdrawn from Sunday's French Grand Prix because he needs further rest after surgery for a sinus infection, his spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The veteran Benetton driver, who has undergone surgery on his sinuses twice in the last month, plans to return for the British Grand Prix at Silverstone on July 13.</p>
